70_TCR_analysis
================

Downstream clone-level analysis for TCR data, mirroring the structure and
plotting conventions of 60_PC_clones / 61_memory_clones (BCR), but adapted
to what's biologically valid for T cells.

Why this isn't a 1:1 copy of the BCR pipeline
----------------------------------------------
The BCR downstream stages (45_immcantation, 45_changeo, 48_GCtree,
60_PC_clones, 61_memory_clones) exist to reconstruct germline sequences and
somatic hypermutation (SHM), which is what makes lineage trees (GCtree),
mutational load, and isotype-switch analyses meaningful for B cells.
T cells don't undergo SHM or class switching, so there is no TCR equivalent
of changeo/germline reconstruction or GCtree lineage trees. Clonal identity
for TCR instead comes directly from scRepertoire's CTstrict (paired
TRA + TRB CDR3 nucleotide sequence), which is already computed in
20_VDJ/out/combined.TCR.filtered.rds (see 20_VDJ/script/TCR_make_combined.filtered.R
and TCR_scRepetorie.R).

So this folder reproduces the *analytical content* that carries over cleanly:
general clone-size figures, diversity analysis (rarefaction/Hill numbers,
Gini, D50/D20), and clonal sharing across compartments — using CTstrict as
the clone identifier instead of clone_subgroup_id_90_similarity, and TRBV
gene usage as the "isotype-analog" categorical variable (in place of isotype
pie charts, since TCR has no isotypes).

Scripts
-------
01_prep_TCR_clone_data.R   Flattens 20_VDJ/out/combined.TCR.filtered.rds into
                            one row per cell, re-derives sample_clean /
                            sample_clean_fol / patient_id using the same
                            suffix-stripping rules as BCR_01_make_combined.filtered.R
                            (so compartment names line up with the existing
                            sample_clean_plot_colors palette), joins in
                            L1_annotation from the integrated Seurat object,
                            and filters to Tfh_cells. Writes RDS files to
                            70_TCR_analysis/out/rds/.

02_TCR_general_figures.R   N clones per compartment, clone-size frequency
                            plot, TRBV gene usage barplot, APackOfTheClones /
                            circle-packing views of clone sizes.

03_TCR_diversity_analysis.R  Clonal abundance curve, Hill-number diversity
                            curve, Shannon diversity per compartment, D50/D20
                            dominance, Gini coefficient — single patient and
                            combined, via alakazam (same functions as
                            60_PC_clones/07_PC_diversity_analysis.R).

04_TCR_clonal_sharing.R    How many compartments each clone is seen in,
                            clonal-sharing proportions, and a pie-chart grid
                            of TRBV usage per compartment-shared clone
                            (isotype-pie analog), via
                            60_PC_clones/08_PC_clonal_sharing.R.

Before running
--------------
Every script has a NOTES/ASSUMPTIONS block at the top. In particular:

- SEURAT_OBJ_PATH and the cell_id join logic in 01_prep_TCR_clone_data.R are
  a best guess based on the join pattern used in
  60_PC_clones/05_PC_general_figures.R (APackOfTheClones section) — verify
  the barcode/cell_id convention against your actual Seurat object before
  trusting the join.
- CELL_TYPE_FILTER defaults to "Tfh_cells" (the T cell L1_annotation label
  used elsewhere in this project, e.g. finer_annotation/ and
  10_broad_annotation/script/color_palette.R). Change it if you want a
  different T cell subset.
- The site filter used for clonal sharing/diversity defaults to comparing
  follicles within SI-PP (Tfh dynamics within Peyer's patch follicles), not
  "LP" as in 60_PC_clones (which is specifically about PC dissemination to
  the lamina propria). Adjust SITE_PATTERN at the top of 03/04 if you want a
  different comparison.
- CTgene's exact string format (which V/J genes end up in which position)
  should be spot-checked once against a few real rows before trusting the
  TRBV-extraction regex in 02/04.
